VTOCLS(1)                      ZOAU Command Syntax                     VTOCLS(1)

NAME

	vtocls - List the contents of the VTOC for a given volume.

SYNOPSIS

	vtocls [-dhuv] <volume> [<dataset>]*

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-u
		Include last reference (usage) time in output.
		Unreferenced datasets listed as January 1st, Year 0.

	-v
		Print out verbose command information.

DESCRIPTION

	vtocls lists the volume table of contents (VTOC) for a given volume,
	filtering by an optional list of datasets.

	Note: If a filter dataset is not in the volume, a message
	will be printed and all subsequent filters will be ignored.

EXAMPLES

	List the contents of volume USER10:

		vtocls USER10

	List the contents of volume USER10, restricted to two datasets,
	and include the last reference time (usage) in the output:

		vtocls -u USER10 ibmuser.user.jcl ibmuser.user.cobol

EXIT VALUES

	0
		At least one dataset was found matching a dataset-pattern

	1
		No datasets were found.

	other
		Error in dataset listing. See error messages for details.
